# ADR-002: Authentication for Login and Sign-up

## Status: Accepted (Date: October 26 2026)

## Context
Gaarp needs individual accounts for personal features
such as watchlists and portfolios. Collaboration features will also
need to associate access and contributions with individual users.

## Decision
We will impliment Supabase to provide authentication for login and sign up.
Application features that require a looged in user will use the authenticated
user identity to associate data with that user's account.

## Consequences
Positive: A managed authentication service avoids maintaining a custom
  credential system.
Positive: A consistent user identity supports user specific data and
 collaboration features.
Negative: Authentication depends on an external service and requires
  configuring its credentials, access policies, and application integration.
